rain-core: xray/0058-muxcool-dial-retry-contract
Source: ReClash test fix on top of xray/0051 and xray/0057 (GPL-3.0).

Three mux.cool tests still assumed that the initiating DialContext always
observes the first carrier dial error. 0051 intentionally retries the first
dial failure immediately (dialBackoff returns zero for the first failure), so
when runDial clears p.dialing before the caller re-enters openContext the
pool performs that retry itself and the caller can succeed transparently.
The old assertions flaked under a loaded race loop: roughly 1/67 for
TestPoolDoesNotRetainFailedCarrierDial, 1/95 for
TestCarrierLimiterReleasesFailedDialReservation and 1/107 for
TestPoolStatsCountsDialFailures.

The tests now follow the 0051 contract without weakening the invariants:

- TestPoolDoesNotRetainFailedCarrierDial accepts the error or the
  transparent success, and still requires exactly two dialer calls, one
  recorded dial failure, no worker for the failed dial and the one
  successful carrier.
- TestCarrierLimiterReleasesFailedDialReservation accepts either outcome and
  still requires the released limiter slot to carry the next successful
  dial after exactly two dialer calls.
- TestPoolStatsCountsDialFailures counts the dials the inline dialer
  actually performed (one or two) and requires Stats().DialFailures to match
  that count with no pending opens.

Test-only: 0051's production semantics are unchanged.

Tests: TestPoolDoesNotRetainFailedCarrierDial,
TestCarrierLimiterReleasesFailedDialReservation,
TestPoolStatsCountsDialFailures.
